-extends "channels/channel_claim_form.html"
-load i18n compress temba

-block pre-form
  -blocktrans trimmed with name=brand.name
    You can connect a <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/live-chat-software/">FreshChat</a> account to your {{ name}}
    account to automate sending and receiving messages via FreshChat. This will also support Apple Business Chat if
    it's been configured on your FreshChat account.

  .mt-4
    -blocktrans trimmed with format='<div class="code inline py-1">channel-uuid/user-uuid</div>'
      Each message sent to the channel will have a URN in the format {{ format }} where the channel UUID is the FreshChat channel's UUID.

  %ol.steps.card
    %li
      -blocktrans trimmed
        In the FreshChat web interface, go to Settings > API Tokens, then select Generate Token. Once the token is
        created, enter it below.
    %li
      -blocktrans trimmed
        Under Settings, select Webhooks, copy the public key and paste it below. This ensures all webhook requests
        from FreshChat will be authenticated.
    %li
      -blocktrans trimmed
        Lastly, you'll need the UUID of the agent that {{ name }} will use when sending FreshChat messages. This is
        available via the <a href="https://developers.freshchat.com/api/#agent">FreshChat API</a>.
    %li
      -blocktrans trimmed
        Once you submit the form, the confirmation page will give you the URL to use for the FreshChat webhooks. Enter
        this URL on the Settings page, under Webhooks, where the Public Key was copied.

-block extra-style
  {{ block.super }}

  :css
    .info {
      width: 800px;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    .form-group {
      margin-bottom:15px;
    }

    #id_auth_token {
      width: 340px;
    }
